{
 "gdd": "2d-lighting-and-occlusion",
 "blocking": [
  "LO-15 default texture layout (L231, L241) / AC-LO-72 / AC-LO-78 (L1417) / LO-32 spike step 2: [main review, raised to BLOCKING by creative-director] The GDD contradicts itself here, and this is the second pass in a row it has been flagged. L231 sets the default layout as 'narrow, beacon, split: the art bible square'. L241, in the same rule, shows those squares fail the axial fit (392.4 > 384, 344.3 > 336). AC-LO-78 says boot must fail with a named error for 'a texture layout failing the' fit tests. So the shipped defaults cannot boot under the GDD's own acceptance criteria, and an implementer cannot satisfy LO-15 and AC-LO-72/78 together. Last pass the arithmetic was added but the default was not changed. FIX: Change the default now to a layout that passes: either the square side grown to A (D_tex drops about 2 %: narrow and beacon 5.33 to 5.22, split 6.10 to 5.95) or the tight box for all five shapes. Restate D.9 to D.11 at the new D_tex, marked ESTIMATE. Keep spike step 2 as the confirmer. Say explicitly that the art-bible square is not a bootable default.",
  "LO-5 / LO-18(ii) / LO-20 / LO-34 / D.13 vs Attention AT-20 (attention-system.md L170, L256, L1774): [main review, raised to BLOCKING by creative-director] The two GDDs disagree. Attention says three times that the DOCK_STATUS pod glow is 'never a tell carrier' and cites LO-20 as the authority. Lighting has 0 occurrences of 'DOCK', and LO-20 exempts only EMERGENCY, so by Lighting's own rules the dock glow gutters on L2/L3 at a tell. A system-switched glow that dips with the web's lean is a false tell. That breaks the honest-signal contract the gutter rules exist to protect, in the room where the player learns to read the baseline (see L54's 'must not be able to confuse' clause). LO-34 still calls the decision 'Attention's call' even though Attention has already made it. FIX: Under G6, Attention's rule is the spec. Name FIXTURE subkind DOCK_STATUS beside EMERGENCY as exempt from L2/L3 (L1 only) in LO-5, LO-18(ii), LO-20 and D.13. Change LO-34 to 'exempt (AT-20)'. Add DOCK_STATUS to AC-LO-25's exemption stubs. Grep horror-entities.md HE-35 for the same exemption."
 ]
}

input.command:
cd /tmp && cat > c.js <<'E'
const M=8;
for (const [name,reach] of [["narrow/beacon",384],["split",336]]) for (const [tex,lim] of [["B",2048],["A",1024]]) {
 const e = tex==="B"?2:1; const A=(reach+M)/(1-e/lim); const D=lim/A;
 console.log(name,tex,"A=",A.toFixed(3),"D=",D.toFixed(4),"edge_tex=",(reach*D).toFixed(1),"scale=",(A/lim).toFixed(5),"a_tex=",(A/2).toFixed(2),"band=",(e/D).toFixed(4));
}
const An=392/(1-2/2048), As=344/(1-2/2048);
const DB=2048/An, DA=1024/(392/(1-1/1024)), DBs=2048/As, DAs=1024/(344/(1-1/1024));
console.log("DB",DB,"DA",DA,"DBs",DBs,"DAs",DAs);
console.log("narrow wB",[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8].map(k=>Math.max(1,2*k/DB).toFixed(2)).join(" / "));
console.log("split wB",[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8].map(k=>Math.max(1,2*k/DBs).toFixed(2)).join(" / "));
console.log("narrow k/D",[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8].map(k=>(k/DB).toFixed(3)).join(" / "), "D/k", [1,2,3,4,5].map(k=>(DB/k).toFixed(2)).join(" / "));
console.log("split k/D",[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8].map(k=>(k/DBs).toFixed(3)).join(" / "));
console.log("errA", 0.5+0.5/DA, "+0.1", 0.6+0.5/DA, "errB",1.5/DB,"n3",0.5+1.5/DA,"n4",0.5+2/DA);
console.log("split errA",0.5+0.5/DAs,"errB",1.5/DBs);
console.log("lat narrow",An/2,80.1+2/DB+8,"beacon",131.6+2/DB+8,"split",As/2,158.3+2/DBs+8, "ax", 384+2/DB+8, 336+2/DBs+8);
E
node c.js

